# Keep the build context small and avoid copying host build artifacts / secrets.
#
# IMPORTANT: no trailing slashes on directory rules. Docker tolerates them, but
# `az acr build` compiles each rule to its own regex — "mobile/" becomes
# ^mobile/$ — and tests it against paths like "mobile". A trailing slash
# therefore matches nothing, silently, and the directory is uploaded anyway.
# Rules starting with **/ only match nested paths (^.*/bin$), so anything that
# can also sit at the repo root needs a bare entry too.

# Build output
**/bin
**/obj
**/dist
**/.vite
bin
obj
dist
frontend/dist

# Dependencies
**/node_modules
node_modules

# Python (Whisper sidecar, not part of this image)
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
whisper-service/.venv

# Local databases — never ship one into the image
**/App_Data
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
.env
.env.*

# Not needed by the Dockerfile (it builds frontend/ and backend/ only)
mobile
whisper-service

# Tooling / VCS. .claude can contain git worktrees, which are large.
.git
.github
.claude
*.md
